// SR 211.432.2 — Chapter 2 Content of the Official Cadastral Survey
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 5 Components of the official cadastral survey
1 The components of the official cadastral survey are:
a. the data;
b. the fixed point and border point markers on the terrain (point markers);
c. the technical and administrative documents;
d. the components and principles of the cadastral survey under the previous system;
2 The DDPS shall regulate the details, in particular the products derived from the official cadastral survey data. Article 7 is reserved.
|

:NOTE
Art. 5 — Amended by No I of the O of 23 Aug. 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2023 529).
|

:INFO
Art. 6 Geodata model for official cadastral surveying
1 The DDPS shall define the requirements for the geodata model for official cadastral surveying, in particular with regard to content, dimensions, accuracy and reliability. The geodata model may have a modular structure.
2 Cantonal extensions to the geodata model are not permitted.
|

:NOTE
Art. 6 — Amended by No I of the O of 23 Aug. 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2023 529).
|

:INFO
Art. 6a
Inserted by No I of the O of 21 May 2008 (AS 2008 2745). Repealed by No 1 of the O of 23 Aug. 2023, with effect from 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2023 529).
|

:INFO
Art. 6bis
Inserted by No I of the O of 7 March 2003 (AS 2003 507). Repealed by No I of the O of 21 May 2008, with effect from 1 July 2008 (AS 2008 2745).
|

:INFO
Art. 7 Land register plan
1 The land register plan is an analogue or digital extract from the official cadastral survey data.
2 It shall contain as a minimum the data on:
a. the border points and boundary lines of the land or buildings (Art. 943 para. 1 no 1 CC);
b. the border points and boundary lines of distinct and permanent rights to immovable property that have been defined in terms of area (Art. 943 para. 1 no 2 CC);
c. mines (Art. 943 para. 1 no. 3 CC);
d. areas subject to continuous movement (Art. 660a CC).
3 The minimum content of the plan has the effect of being recorded in the land register (Art. 971-974 CC).
4 The cantons may, in addition to the official cadastral survey data, require boundaries of easements to be indicated, provided their positions are clearly defined on the ground.
|

:INFO
Art. 7 (continued)
5 The Federal Department of Justice and Police (FDJP) and the DDPS shall jointly determine the requirements for the land register plan and other extracts, in particular with regard to content and presentation.
|

:NOTE
Art. 7 — Amended by No I of the O of 23 Aug. 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2023 529).
|

:INFO
Art. 8–9
Repealed by No I of the O of 7 March 2003, with effect from 1 April 2003 (AS 2003 507).
|

:INFO
Art. 10
Repealed by No I of the O of 23 March 2023, with effect from 1 April 2024 (AS 2023 529).

